      "side": 1,
      "message": "Seems a bit too cryptic to me.\n\n\n\n```suggestion\nWhen an externally updated `tables.list` causes `addReftable()` \nto fail, the system triggers a stack reload. Previously, this \nreload occurred before obtaining the cached-reader lock.\n\nThis lock inversion was unsafe. The reload operation could close \na table that was concurrently being read by a ref lookup, which \nresulted in a `ClosedChannelException`.\n\nFix this by acquiring the cached-reader lock before reloading the \nstack. This ensures that tables remain open and safe to access \nwhile concurrent threads are actively reading them.\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "3aa0700a6b7efc41b426ccae67fc8c79c4d35b51",
